  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There is a tech park, which consists of NNN rooms, numbered 1,2,…,N1, 2, \\ldots, N1,2,…,N. The iii-th room has a cost of AiA_iAi​ associated with it. There are MMM bi-directional passages between these rooms.\n\nChef wants to create an office in this tech park, for which she will select exactly KKK out of these NNN rooms. These KKK rooms must be selected such that every selected room is reachable from every other selected room using some number of passages, and without passing through an unselected room.\n\nThe cost of creating the office is **not** the sum of the individual costs of the rooms, but rather the difference of the bitwise ORs and bitwise ANDs of the individual costs of the KKK rooms. \n\nFormally, let x1,x2,x3,...,xKx_1, x_2, x_3, ..., x_Kx1​,x2​,x3​,...,xK​ be the selected rooms. The cost of creating the office is (Ax1∣Ax2∣…∣AxK)(A_{x_1} | A_{x_2} | \\ldots | A_{x_K})(Ax1​​∣Ax2​​∣…∣AxK​​) - (Ax1&amp;Ax2&amp;…&amp;AxK)(A_{x_1} \\&amp; A_{x_2}  \\&amp; \\ldots \\&amp; A_{x_K})(Ax1​​&amp;Ax2​​&amp;…&amp;AxK​​), \n\nwhere '∣|∣' represents the bitwise OR operator, and '&amp;\\&amp;&amp;' represents the bitwise AND operator.\n\nWhat is the minimum cost that must be incurred to create this office, if Chef selects the KKK rooms optimally? If it is not possible to select KKK rooms satisfying the given conditions, print −1-1−1.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains three space-separated integers NNN, MMM and KKK — the number of rooms, passages and required number of rooms in the office respectively.\nThe next line contains NNN integers, A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, denoting the cost associated with each of the rooms.\nThe next MMM lines describe the passages. The iii-th of these MMM lines contains two space-separated integers, uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​, denoting a passage between rooms uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum possible cost for that test case. Or output -1 if it is not possible to select KKK rooms.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "1≤K≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq K \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot10^51≤K≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤M≤min(2⋅105,N⋅(N−1)2)0 \\leq M \\leq min(2\\cdot10^5, \\frac{N\\cdot(N-1)}{2})0≤M≤min(2⋅105,2N⋅(N−1)​)",
      "0≤Ai≤1090 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^90≤Ai​≤109",
      "1≤ui,vi≤N1 \\leq u_i, v_i \\leq N1≤ui​,vi​≤N",
      "ui≠viu_i \\neq v_iui​=vi​ for each 1≤i≤M1 \\leq i \\leq M1≤i≤M.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot10^52⋅105.",
      "The sum of MMM over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot10^52⋅105."
    ],
